{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Ya3EXGAFcDwxiBHYnitmHf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted data for each planned experiment in the experiment plan, under the \"best\" tier definition. I need to produce a single YAML block with all the imagined experiments, including expected results, rationales, tables, figures, and analysis.\n\nLet me carefully go through each plan_001 through plan_014 and generate predictions consistent with the \"best\" tier metrics and narrative.\n\nKey metrics from \"best\" tier:\n- baseline_gsm8k: [81, 85]\n- rasp_post_prune_gsm8k: [26, 32]\n- standard_post_prune_gsm8k: [0, 3]\n\n\n- graspune_post_prune_gsm8k: [12, 22]\n- rasp_sft_grpo_recovered_gsm8k: [65, 78]\n- standard_sft_grpo_recovered_gsm8k: [5, 18]\n- graspune_sft_grpo_recovered_gsm8k: [30, 50]\n- multi_seed_rasp_post_prune_stddev: [0, 3]\n- cka_recoverability_mixed_effects_r2: [0.25, 0.45]\n- recovery_method_x_pruning_interaction_p: (continuing to review the remaining metrics)\n\nNow I'm mapping out concrete predictions for each experimental plan using values within these ranges. For the baseline full GSM8K evaluation, I'm expecting around 83.2% accuracy, with RASP_20 dropping to roughly 29.3% post-pruning and Standard_20 falling to about 1.4%. After SFT warmup, RASP_20 should recover to around 48% and Standard_20 to approximately 14%, both within their respective recovery ranges. Moving into the GRPO recovery phase to see how much further these models can improve.\n\nFor the GRPO-recovered models, I'm projecting RASP_20 reaches around 72% accuracy and Standard_20 climbs to roughly 12%. Plan 004 will run the full 1319-sample evaluation on these recovered models. With GRASPrune at 20% pruning, I expect post-prune performance around 17%, then recovering to about 41% after SFT and GRPO. The multi-seed RASP_20 experiments show relatively tight variance across se