t      ensuring ≥40% MLP capacity per layer. Actual sparsity: Standard=33.02%, RASP=33.21%.\n120\t      MLP range both [8128,18944]. GSM8K@100 results: Standard=0.0% (0/100), RASP=1.0%\n121\t      (1/100). v2 had 0.15% with min_keep_mlp=4. The capacity floor preserved more\n122\t      MLP width but did not rescue reasoning ability. Model outputs remain degenerate\n123\t      (repeated digits, empty strings, repetition loops). 35% structured sparsity\n124\t      fundamentally destroys too much model capacity for this architecture. Next steps:\n125\t      (1) try 20-25% sparsity, (2) add post-prune recovery fine-tuning (the actual\n126\t      RASP hypothesis), or (3) semi-structured pruning.'\n127\t  mvp_rasp_pipeline_v4:\n128\t    status: PREPARING\n129\t    retry_count: 0\n130\t    created_at: '2026-05-14T15:14:18.821Z'\n131\t    updated_at: '2026-05-14T17:53:39.178Z'\n132\t    hypothesis: 'CKA functional overlap F(h) predicts structured pruning recoverability\n133\t      under RLVR. RASP scoring S(h)=I(h)×(1-F(h))^α selects structures whose removal\n134\t      is more recoverable via GRPO RLVR than standard importance-only pruning. V4:\n135\t      Dual sparsity probe (20% + 25%) to find viable operating point where pruned\n136\t      models retain >5% accuracy, then GRPO recovery comparison.'\n137\t    parent: mvp_rasp_pipeline_v3\n138\t    notes: 'GSM8K eval (100 samples, max_new_tokens=4096) partial results:\n139\t\n140\t      - baseline (Qwen2.5-7B): 94% (eval_baseline_7b_quick_fixed.json)\n141\t\n142\t      - rasp_20: 29% (eval_pruned_rasp_20_quick.json)\n143\t\n144\t      - standard_20: 1% (eval_pruned_standard_20_quick.json)\n145\t\n146\t      - standard_25: INCOMPLETE (killed at 72/100 by GRPO training OOM)\n147\t\n148\t      - rasp_25: NOT STARTED (GRPO training took GPUs)\n149\t\n150\t      Key finding: RASP 20% pruning retains 29% vs standard 1% — 29x advantage. GRPO\n151\t      recovery training now running on both GPUs (recovered_rasp_20 on GPU0, recovered_standard_20\n152\t      on GPU1). standard_25 and rasp_25 eval need re-run after training completes.'\n153\t  grpo_rasp_20:\n154\t    status: DONE\n155\t    retry_count: 0\n156\t    created_at: '2026-05-14T17:08:34.784Z'\n157\t    updated_at: '2026-05-14T17:37:57.217Z'\n158\t    spec:\n159\t      command: bash src/run_grpo_v4.sh rasp 20 0\n160\t      server: westb-23072\n161\t      gpu:\n162\t      - cuda:0\n163\t      pid: '221261'\n164\t      log_path: ~/runs/recovery_aware_struct_prune/grpo_rasp_20.log\n165\t      submitted_at: '2026-05-14T17:08:34.775Z'\n166\t      submitted_via: submit_training_job\n167\t      backend: tmux\n168\t      account: root\n169\t      data_path: GSM8K train (8792 samples)\n170\t      data_count: 8792\n171\t      model_name: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B (pruned RASP 20%)\n172\t      seed: 42\n173\t      checkpoint_source: /root/autodl-tmp/pruned_rasp_20\n174\t      model_path: /root/autodl-tmp/pruned_rasp_20\n175\t      output_dir: /root/autodl-tmp/recovered_rasp_20\n176\t      gpu_model: RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell 94GB\n177\t      wall_clock_seconds: 1762.4\n178\t      gpu_hours: 0.49\n179\t    hypothesis: RASP-pruned model (20% sparsity, post-prune 29% GSM8K) recovers better\n180\t      under GRPO RLVR than standard-pruned model (20% sparsity, post-prune 1% GSM8K).\n181\t      Both have identical total MLP params (395,232) — difference is purely from distribution\n182\t      strategy (Scenario B).\n183\t    parent: mvp_rasp_pipeline_v4\n184\t    conclusion: killed\n185\t    completed_at: '2026-05-14T17:37:57.217Z'\n186\t  grpo_standard_20:\n187\t    status: DONE\n188\t    retry_count: 0\n189\t    created_at: '2026-05-14T17:11:33.478Z'\n190\t    updated_at: '2026-05-14T17:37:57.677Z'\n191\t    spec:\n192\t      command: bash src/run_grpo_v4.sh standard 20 1\n193\t      server: westb-23072\n194\t      gpu:\n195\t      - cuda:1\n196\t      pid: '221901'\n197\t      log_path: ~/runs/recovery_aware_struct_prune/grpo_standard_20.log\n198\t 