{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Grq38H1uuBXWm7ctAsRR2q","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have all the information needed. Let me create a comprehensive summary:\n\n## Summary: Experiment Results, Configs, and Scoring Details\n\n### 1. **Experiment Results (GSM8K Evaluation)**\n\n**Baseline & Post-Prune Evaluations (100-sample quick eval on DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B):**\n\n| Model | Sparsity | GSM8K Accuracy | Status | Notes |\n|-------|----------|------------------|---------|-------|\n| Baseline (Qwen2.5-7B) | 0% | 94% | Reference | eval_baseline_7b_quick_fixed.json |\n| RASP 20% (post-prune) | 20% | 29% (29/100) | ✓ Complete | RASP structure selection preserves reasoning |\n| Standard 20% (post-prune) | 20% | 1% (1/100) | ✓ Complete | Importance-only pruning collapses capability |\n| RASP 25% | 25% | Not started | Incomplete | GRPO training consumed GPUs |\n| Standard 25% | 25% | Killed at 72/100 | Incomplete | OOM during parallel GRPO training |\n| Standard 35% | 35% | 0% | Failed | min_keep_mlp=4 destroyed early-layer representations (14.3% MLP capacity) |\n| RASP 35% | 35% | 0% | Failed | Too aggressive for distilled model; distillation removed redundancy |\n\n**Key Finding:** RASP achieves **29x advantage** (29% vs 1%) at 20% sparsity, demonstrating the value of structure selection for recoverability.\n\n**GRPO Recovery Training Results:**\n- **grpo_rasp_20**: Trained with fast config (max_length=1024), killed after 500 steps with zero gradient signal — truncation artifact, not true convergence\n- **grpo_rasp_20_4096**: D010 attempt with max_completion_length=4096, failed with process crashes (no W&B sentinel)\n- **grpo_standard_20_fast**: Zero reward throughout training (expected: negative control)\n- All GRPO runs inconclusive due to infrastructure issues (token length, memory, process stability)\n\n---\n\n### 2. **RASP Scoring Formula Details**\n\n**Core Formula** (rasp_scoring.py, line 23-40):\n```python\nS(h) = I(h) * (1 - F(h))^alpha\n```\n\nWhere:\n- **S(h)**: Final pruning score (ascending sort = prune first)\n- **I(h)**: Gradient-based importance (Taylor expansion) = `||w_h * grad_h||_2`\n- **F(h)**: Functional overlap (linear CKA) in [0, 1]\n- **alpha**: Recoverability penalty exponent (default=1.0)\n\n**Interpretation:**\n- Heads with **high overlap** (F(h) close to 1) are penalized: `(1-F(h))^alpha ≈ 0`\n- Even important heads (high I(h)) with high F(h) get low scores → retained (delayed pruning)\n- Structures with low redundancy (low F(h)) and low importance are pruned first\n\n**CKA Computation** (cka_overlap.py):\n\n1. **Linear CKA formula** (line 38-47):\n   ```python\n   X, Y: [n_samples, dim]\n   X = X - X.mean(0)  # center\n   Y = Y - Y.mean(0)\n   HSIC_XY = ||X^T Y||_Fro^2\n   HSIC_XX = ||X^T X||_Fro^2\n   HSIC_YY = ||Y^T Y||_Fro^2\n   CKA = HSIC_XY / (sqrt(HSIC_XX) * sqrt(HSIC_YY))\n   ```\n\n2. **Per-structure F(h)** (line 176-202):\n   - Compute pairwise CKA between all structures (heads/groups)\n   - F(h) = mean CKA with other structures = (row_sum - 1.0) / (n_structures - 1)\n   - This is mean **intra-layer** functional overlap\n\n3. **Activation Collection:**\n   - **Attention heads**: Mean-pooled q_proj output per head across sequence (line 112-120)\n     - Input: [batch, seq_len, n_heads*head_dim]\n     - Output per sample: [n_heads, head_dim]\n   - **MLP groups**: Mean-pooled gate_proj output, grouped into 28 channel groups (line 126-173)\n     - Group size: `intermediate_size / n_heads = 18944 / 28 = 676`\n     - Output per sample: [n_groups, group_size]\n\n4. **Calibration Data**: GSM8K train (512 samples default, max_length=512)\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Importance Score Details** (importance_score.py)\n\n**Gradient-based Taylor Expansion**: I(h) = ||w_h * ∇w_h||_2\n\n**Per-Structure Computation:**\n- **Attention heads** (line 84-128):\n  - Incorporate: q_proj, k_proj, v_proj, o_proj\n  - GQA handling: k_proj and v_proj have `num_key_value_heads=4`, broadcast to full 28 query heads\n  - Per-head L2 norm: `taylor.view(n_heads, -1).norm(dim=1)`\n\n- **MLP groups** (line 130-150):\n  - Incorporate: gate_proj, up_proj (both shape [intermediate, hidden])\n  - Grouping: n_groups = 28 = n_attention_heads\n  - Per-group L2 norm: `taylor.view(n_groups, -1).norm(dim=1)`\n\n**Averaging**: Over calibration batches (accumulated importance ÷ n_samples)\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Model Architecture: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B**\n\n**Key Parameters:**\n- **num_hidden_layers**: 32\n- **num_attention_heads**: 28\n- **num_key_value_heads**: 4 (Grouped Query Attention)\n- **heads_per_kv_group**: 7 (28 ÷ 4)\n- **hidden_size**: 3,584 (28 heads × 128 dim/head)\n- **head_dim**: 128\n- **intermediate_size** (FFN per-layer): 18,944\n- **MLP groups** (for pruning): 28 (same as num_attention_heads)\n- **MLP group_size**: 676 (18944 ÷ 28)\n\n**Total Parameters**: ~5.99B (consistent with 7B distilled claim; smaller than full models due to knowledge distillation)\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Evaluation Setup**\n\n**GSM8K Test Evaluation** (eval_gsm8k.py):\n- **Dataset**: OpenAI GSM8K test split (1,319 samples for full eval; 100 used in quick tests)\n- **Prompt Format**:\n  ```\n  Solve the following math problem step by step. Put your final answer in \\boxed{}.\n  Question: {q}\n  Answer:\n  ```\n- **Answer Extraction**:\n  1. Try `\\boxed{...}` (LaTeX format)\n  2. Fall back to `####` pattern (GSM8K gold format)\n  3. Fall back to last numeric value in response\n- **Normalization**: Remove commas, handle floats vs ints\n- **Metrics**: Accuracy = correct / total\n\n**Key Parameters**:\n- `max_new_tokens`: 512 (standard) or 4096 (for R1 long CoT reasoning)\n- `temperature`: 0.0 (greedy decoding)\n- Batch size: 1 (to match production inference)\n\n---\n\n### 6. **File Locations**\n\n**Source Code**:\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/src/rasp_scoring.py` — RASP formula\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/src/cka_overlap.py` — CKA computation\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/src/importance_score.py` — Importance scoring\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/src/prune.py` — Pruning execution\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/src/eval_gsm8k.py` — Evaluation script\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/src/grasp_scoring.py` — GRASPrune baseline (planned)\n\n**Configuration & Plans**:\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/experiment_plan.yaml` — Full experimental roadmap (P0-P2)\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/registry.yaml` — Experiment run log with status/failures\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/memory.md` — GRASPrune baseline research memo\n\n**Logs & Results**:\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/logs/workers/` — Worker task logs\n- Results embedded in registry.yaml (direct JSON inline, not separate files)\n\n---\n\n### 7. **Critical Implementation Notes**\n\n1. **GQA Group Constraint**: Pruning must preserve divisibility — when all Q heads mapped to a KV head are pruned, that KV head is also removed (prune.py line 88-93)\n\n2. **MLP Grouping Strategy**: \n   - n_groups = 28 (matches n_attention_heads for symmetry)\n   - Each group has 676 channels\n   - **Per-layer capacity floor** (from v3 fix): min_keep_mlp ≥ max(4, int(n_mlp_groups * 0.4)) = 12 groups per layer\n\n3. **Sparsity Sweet Spot for Distilled Model**: \n   - 35% → 0% accuracy (too aggressive, destroys representations)\n   - 20% → 29% RASP vs 1% Standard (viable operating point)\n   - 25% → Not conclusively tested (interrupted)\n\n4. **CKA Calibration**: \n   - Uses GSM8K train (512 samples)\n   - Mean-pools activations over sequence dimension\n   - Computes intra-layer pairwise similarities only\n\n5. **Alpha Parameter**: \n   - Default α=1.0 (linear penalty)\n   - Controls recoverability weight\n   - Not yet ablated in experiments"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50085846-2f4c-49ad-8f2d-ef8b9b74cc58","uuid":"6bc3b1b2-d2a1-44cd-af6b-63e004aba571","timestamp":"2026-05-14T23:45:55.281Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17, find all files related to experiment results, configs, and scoring. I need to understand:\n1. What experiment results exist (look for JSON/YAML result files, logs)\n2. The RASP scoring formula details (alpha parameter, CKA computation)\n3. Any existing eval results (GSM8K scores, post-prune metrics)\n4. The model architecture details (number of heads, layers for DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B)\n\nSearch broadly: experiment_results, results, eval, scoring, config files. Look in subdirectories like experiments/, results/, configs/, src/, etc.","agentId":"a4babd18a588f976e","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have all the information needed. Let me create a comprehensive summary:\n\n## Summary: Experiment Results, Configs, and Scoring Details\n\n### 1. **Experiment Results (GSM8K Evaluation)**\n\n**Baseline & Post-Prune Evaluations (100-sample quick eval on DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B):**\n\n| Model | Sparsity | GSM8K Accuracy | Status | Notes |\n|-------|----------|------------------|---------|-------|\n| Baseline (Qwen2.5-7B) | 0% | 94% | Reference | eval_baseline_7b_quick_fixed.json |\n| RASP 20% (post-prune) | 20% | 29% (29/100) | ✓ Complete | RASP structure selection preserves reasoning |\n| Standard 20% (post-prune) | 20% | 1% (1/100) | ✓ Complete | Importance-only pruning collapses capability |\n| RASP 25% | 25% | Not started | Incomple